# A VexelRay desktop application. This is the reference one.
#
# It began as the shape calculator-vexel-demo taught -- the application edge, the
# threading model, the build, and the two documents a project of this kind keeps.
# The hand-wired ports were deleted on purpose (keeping them ported cost a tax on
# every framework change), and Calculator, VexelRay IDE and MainFrame were later rebuilt
# from this template rather than the other way round. So the shape is copied from
# nowhere. It is stated here, and this tree is what the framework is verified
# against rather than a sketch of something else.
#
# What a new project is, is a small text editor: tabs over the files it has open, a
# navigator over a folder, and Markdown shown in colour. An editor because it is the
# smallest real application that reaches every seam a real one does -- the clock
# (every widget here moves), spans, work off the frame loop (every read and write),
# a close gate (unsaved files), the settings store (the session comes back), and a
# tree that can be built and tested with no window. It uses nothing native beyond
# what the framework brings, so it builds wherever the framework does. It replaced a
# counter, which reached almost none of those, and made the framework look like it
# was for counters.
#
# Every file this writes is listed below. That is not tidiness -- a bundled
# template's files are classpath resources, and a classpath directory cannot be
# enumerated in a native image, so these lines are the only record of what is in
# it. VexelDesktopTest.theManifestAndTheFolderAgree holds the list and the folder
# together.

template  vexel-desktop
title     VexelRay desktop application
summary   a tabbed text editor with a file navigator: a -core controller and a -gui view, talking by messages
folder    ${artifactId}
next      cd ${artifactId} && mvn compile exec:exec

# ---- what it is ------------------------------------------------------------------

slot where
    label     create it in
    kind      folder
    required  yes
    help      the folder the project folder goes inside -- your checkouts directory

slot artifactId
    label     project name
    kind      text
    required  yes
    preset    my-app
    match     [a-z][a-z0-9]*(-[a-z0-9]+)*
    rule      maven-id
    help      lower case, dashes between words; it is the folder name and the Maven artifactId

slot groupId
    label     group
    kind      text
    required  yes
    preset    dev.example
    match     [a-z][a-z0-9_]*(\.[a-z0-9_]+)*
    rule      maven-id
    help      your Maven groupId, e.g. dev.vexelray.demo

slot version
    label     project version
    kind      text
    required  no
    match     [0-9A-Za-z][0-9A-Za-z._-]*
    help      the project's Maven version; leave blank for the framework's own, the stack it is made against

slot summary
    label     one-line summary
    kind      text
    required  no
    preset    A VexelRay desktop application.
    most      160
    help      goes in the pom and the README

# ---- the names inside it ---------------------------------------------------------

slot packageName
    label     java package
    kind      text
    required  no
    match     [a-z][a-z0-9_]*(\.[a-z0-9_]+)*
    rule      java-package
    help      leave blank for <group>.<project name>

slot className
    label     main class
    kind      text
    required  no
    match     [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*
    rule      java-type
    help      leave blank for a name made from the project name

slot title
    label     window title
    kind      text
    required  no
    most      60
    help      leave blank to use the project name

slot icon
    label     icon name
    kind      text
    required  no
    match     [a-z][a-z0-9]*(-[a-z0-9]+)*
    help      the mark's file name without .ico, for a project that brings its own; leave blank for the project name

# ---- the window ------------------------------------------------------------------

slot width
    label     window width
    kind      number
    required  yes
    preset    1180
    least     320
    most      8192
    help      in the engine's logical coordinates, on a first run

slot height
    label     window height
    kind      number
    required  yes
    preset    720
    least     240
    most      8192

# ---- the stack it builds against --------------------------------------------------

slot vexelrayVersion
    label     vexelray version
    kind      text
    required  yes
    preset    0.1.3-SNAPSHOT
    help      the version of vexelray, the engine, installed in your local Maven repository

slot tactrollerVersion
    label     tactroller version
    kind      text
    required  yes
    preset    1.3-SNAPSHOT

# ---- what to include ---------------------------------------------------------------

slot tests
    label     starting tests
    kind      flag
    required  no
    preset    yes
    help      unit tests for the editor, the jobs, the file policy, the Markdown spans, the navigator and the real tree headless

slot modules
    label     modules
    kind      text
    required  no
    preset    all
    help      which modules to include: all, none, or their names (examples, later); one comes with those it requires

# ---- the modules -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A module is a set of whole files, taken or left when the project is made, and what it
# adds to a file it shares, in place of a "<!-- part: name -->" line there. Nothing
# inside a file depends on which were taken, and a module names only the base and the
# modules it requires, so a module can break only the base or itself: VexelDesktopTest
# holds both, and the base alone, each module alone and all of them are built
# (docs/plans/template-modules.md). The editor is still the base; it becomes modules
# later in that plan.

module examples
    about     an Examples window (F1) that the worked examples show in, and EXAMPLES.md, their index

module later
    about     do something later, or once the typing stops: a chain's NONE within a time
    requires  examples

# ---- worked out rather than asked for ------------------------------------------------

fill blank  packageName    package  ${groupId}.${artifactId}
fill always packagePath    path     ${packageName}
fill blank  className      type     ${artifactId}
fill blank  title          title    ${artifactId}
fill blank  summary        text     A VexelRay desktop application.
fill blank  icon           text     ${artifactId}
fill always appName        slug     ${artifactId}
# The framework's own version, which vexelray-gui and vexelray-codec move with; the engine and the build
# plugin keep theirs. VexelDesktopTest.theStackIsTheFrameworksOwnVersion holds it to this module's.
fill always frameworkVersion text     0.2.0-SNAPSHOT
fill always guiVersion       text     ${frameworkVersion}
fill always buildVersion     text     ${vexelrayVersion}
fill always codecVersion     text     ${frameworkVersion}
# A new project starts at the version of the stack it was made against: 0.2's projects are 0.2.0-SNAPSHOT.
fill blank  version          text     ${frameworkVersion}
fill always junitVersion   text     5.11.4

# ---- the tree ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A parent and two modules, split where the dependency edge falls. -core is the
# controller: the editor, which decides, and the jobs that touch the disk; it builds
# against no widget, so its tests need no window. -gui is the view and the framework
# integration: the window, the entry point, the wiring and the native build. The two
# talk by messages and nothing else. Everything is run from the parent's folder.

file pom.xml
file ${artifactId}-core/pom.xml                            from core-pom.xml
file ${artifactId}-gui/pom.xml                             from gui-pom.xml
file .gitignore                                            from gitignore
file README.md

# What a coding agent reads before it touches anything: the rules the code does not
# show, and how to check a change by driving the window rather than by compiling it.

file CLAUDE.md
file docs/framework-notes.md
file docs/retrospective.md
file docs/TODO.md

# ---- -core: the controller -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# A file's source is a plain name inside files/, and its path is where it lands, so
# every one of these needs its "from" -- the two are only ever the same for a file
# that sits at the top of the project. Core lists the module's jobs:
# the processor compiling -gui sees only the sources of -gui, and Core, named as a
# starter, is how the wiring hears of the rest.

file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/Core.java        from Core.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/Messages.java    from Messages.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/Editor.java      from Editor.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/Doc.java         from Doc.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/ReadFile.java    from ReadFile.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/WriteFile.java   from WriteFile.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/FindPath.java    from FindPath.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/CreateFile.java  from CreateFile.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/ReadSession.java from ReadSession.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/WriteSession.java from WriteSession.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/ListFolder.java  from ListFolder.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/MarkText.java    from MarkText.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/TextFile.java    from TextFile.java
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/Markdown.java    from Markdown.java

file ${artifactId}-core/src/test/java/${packagePath}/core/DocTest.java      from DocTest.java      when tests
file ${artifactId}-core/src/test/java/${packagePath}/core/EditorTest.java   from EditorTest.java   when tests
file ${artifactId}-core/src/test/java/${packagePath}/core/FilesTest.java    from FilesTest.java    when tests
file ${artifactId}-core/src/test/java/${packagePath}/core/TextFileTest.java from TextFileTest.java when tests
file ${artifactId}-core/src/test/java/${packagePath}/core/MarkdownTest.java from MarkdownTest.java when tests
file ${artifactId}-core/src/test/java/${packagePath}/core/ListFolderTest.java from ListFolderTest.java when tests

# ---- -gui: the view and the framework integration --------------------------------------

file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/${className}.java  from App.java

# The one class the processor reads, @VexelApp's. It names Core, and the automation
# starter in every build, the release one too: the sockets start off, and the title
# bar's plug shows whether they are open and whether anything is or was connected.

file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/${className}App.java  from AppDeclaration.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Recipes.java       from Recipes.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/View.java          from View.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Intent.java        from Intent.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Ui.java            from Ui.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Look.java          from Look.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Type.java          from Type.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Landmarks.java     from Landmarks.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Motion.java        from Motion.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Workspace.java     from Workspace.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Buffer.java        from Buffer.java
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/Navigator.java     from Navigator.java

# The mark, and what a native build needs. The .ico is copied as it is (it is not
# text, so nothing is substituted into it): the window wears it from the class
# path and the executable links it through the .rc, so they are one file. The
# icon slot names it, so a project that brings its mark keeps its file names. The
# .svg is its source; the metadata is this program's own, everything else in a
# native image registers itself.

file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/rc/${icon}.ico             from new-app.ico
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/rc/${icon}.svg             from new-app.svg
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/rc/${artifactId}.rc        from app.rc
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/rc/${artifactId}.manifest  from app.manifest

# The native build needs rc.exe and the MSVC link.exe, which are on PATH only in a
# Visual Studio developer prompt (and under Git Bash coreutils' link.exe shadows the
# linker). This finds vcvars64 with vswhere and runs mvn inside it, in the parent's
# folder, so it builds both modules. It is written with CR LF line endings whatever
# this copy has: see Scaffold.isBatchFile.

file native-build.cmd
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/resources/META-INF/native-image/${groupId}/${artifactId}/reachability-metadata.json  from reachability-metadata.json

file ${artifactId}-gui/src/test/java/${packagePath}/ViewTest.java          from ViewTest.java          when tests
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/test/java/${packagePath}/LookTest.java          from LookTest.java          when tests

# ---- the worked examples ----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# What an application reaches for, each worked out the polished way, in a window of its
# own (F1) so the editor's window stays as it is: docs/plans/template-examples.md is the
# plan. EXAMPLES.md indexes them, question to files, test and ottermate script. Each one is
# a folder in each module and is named nowhere else: every @Configuration in -gui's sources
# is read by the processor, so an example's own configuration adds its -core part and its
# piece of the window, and deleting its folders takes it out. Each example is a module,
# and its row in EXAMPLES.md is a part.

file EXAMPLES.md                                                                  in examples
part CLAUDE.md how-to-work                                                        from examples/claude-how-to-work.md in examples
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/Examples.java       from examples/Examples.java       in examples
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/ExamplesWindow.java from examples/ExamplesWindow.java in examples
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/ExamplesPage.java   from examples/ExamplesPage.java   in examples
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/ExamplesView.java   from examples/ExamplesView.java   in examples
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/ExamplesList.java   from examples/ExamplesList.java   in examples
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/Example.java        from examples/Example.java        in examples
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/test/java/${packagePath}/ExamplesTest.java            from examples/ExamplesTest.java   in examples when tests

# Do something later, or once the typing stops: a chain's NONE within a time.

file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/examples/later/Later.java         from examples/Later.java         in later
file ${artifactId}-core/src/main/java/${packagePath}/core/examples/later/LaterMessages.java from examples/LaterMessages.java in later
file ${artifactId}-core/src/test/java/${packagePath}/core/examples/later/LaterTest.java     from examples/LaterTest.java     in later when tests
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/later/LaterParts.java          from examples/LaterParts.java    in later
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/later/LaterPanel.java          from examples/LaterPanel.java    in later
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/later/LaterNodes.java          from examples/LaterNodes.java    in later
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/main/java/${packagePath}/examples/later/LaterView.java           from examples/LaterView.java     in later
file ${artifactId}-gui/src/test/java/${packagePath}/LaterWindowTest.java                   from examples/LaterWindowTest.java in later when tests
file checks/later.txt                                                                       from examples/later.txt          in later
part EXAMPLES.md rows                                                                       from examples/later-row.md       in later

# ---- what it will not build without ---------------------------------------------------
#
# Looked up in the local Maven repository before anything is written, because this
# stack is installed rather than downloaded and a version nobody has run
# `mvn install` for is the likeliest reason a fresh project does not build. The
# platform modules are deliberately not here: exactly one of them activates from
# the host OS, so checking for all three would warn about two that are correctly
# absent.

needs dev.vexelray.build:vexelray-build-maven-plugin:${buildVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.framework:vexelray-framework-api:${frameworkVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.framework:vexelray-framework-core:${frameworkVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.framework:vexelray-framework-shell:${frameworkVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.framework:vexelray-framework-automation:${frameworkVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.framework:vexelray-framework-processor:${frameworkVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.gui:vexelray-gui-core:${guiVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.gui:vexelray-gui-widget:${guiVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.gui:vexelray-gui-krono:${guiVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.gui:vexelray-gui-automation:${guiVersion}
needs sibarum.tactroller:tactroller-atchung:${tactrollerVersion}
needs sibarum.tactroller:tactroller-clipboard:${tactrollerVersion}
needs dev.vexelray.codec:vexelray-codec-record:${codecVersion}
